          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వైద్యుడు (vaidyuḍu) — \"a doctor, a physician\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Look at the middle of it. vaidya is built on the very vid sitting inside విద్యార్థి (vidyārthi): a physician is one versed in the knowledge, the knowledge in question being आयुर्वेद, the science of long life."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending -ుడు is not Sanskrit's but Telugu's own, marking a masculine person — the same -ుడు already carried by స్నేహితుడు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
