          "title": "You'll want to know: అతిథి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అతిథి (atithi) — \"a guest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a-tithi — \"one without a tithi\", without a date on the calendar. The guest is defined by not being expected."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The old formula అతిథి (atithi) దేవో భవ, \"let the guest be a god to you\", is built on exactly that: you cannot prepare for a god who arrives unannounced, so you keep the house ready instead. What a Telugu house actually does when the అతిథి (atithi) arrives has a chapter of its own, at the end of this book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five roles: a teacher, a student, a doctor, a farmer, a guest."
            }
          ]
        },
